cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LLVM-snippy in your research or verification flow, please cite it using these metadata."

type: software
title: "LLVM-snippy"
abstract: >-
  LLVM-snippy is an LLVM-based instruction sequence generator for low-level
  verification. It generates randomized machine-code test programs from
  configurable inputs and reuses LLVM target descriptions and code-generation
  infrastructure. The project is primarily used for processor verification,
  with a focus on RISC-V and other targets supported by LLVM.

